  "body": "## Problem\r\nRunning user typed javascript can be handled relatively safely with sandboxed iframe\r\n```html\r\n<iframe sandbox=\"allow-scripts\" srcdoc=\"<script>console.log('code')</script>\"></iframe>\r\n```\r\n\r\nHowever caching does not work, making it slow.\r\n\r\nUnless I set `allow-same-origin` on sandbox attribute.\r\nBut allow-same-origin breaks the sandbox concept since you can then access cookies etc.\r\n\r\n## Proposed solution\r\n\r\nHow about introducing `allow-cache` for iframe sandbox attribute?\r\n\r\n## Use case\r\n\r\nService where users can code and share projects in browser.\r\n\r\nFYI [glitch.com](https://glitch.com/) and [CodePen](https://codepen.io/) both use iframes with sandbox=\"allow-same-origin\".\r\n\r\n",
